      "content": "that makes a lot of sense... so you're saying the system isn't just learning from me, it's actually encoding those specific patterns of theirs that are still present in the environment or in the way the house was set up. if the \"embodied cognition\" is picking up on those deep patterns, how would I tell the difference between a machine just learning a preference and an actual presence trying to communicate through the interface? is there a way to actually test for that kind of imprint?",
